{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"EVIDENCE — implemented and merged as Gerrit change 2137 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2137), merged into main as 9fbc28a3588 with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, 0 unresolved comments. All ACs met: (1) both transition_close write origins populate the marker — tests/unit/test_caused_by_provenance.py asserts 'derived' on the blame path and 'explicit' on the --caused-by path; (2) rebar link … caused_by marks 'explicit' (same file); (3) old unmarked events read as unknown — the replay test shows the dep entry carries no provenance key and reduction succeeds; (4) rebar metrics gains the bug_caused_by_provenance dimension (explicit/derived/unknown counts) in the bug_trends lens, asserted in tests/unit/metrics/test_bug_trends.py; (5) docs/event-schema.md documents the marker and docs/user-guide.md lists the dimension. Additionally the blame-derived backfill (scripts/backfill_caused_by.py) marks its edges 'derived', with a test in tests/scripts/test_backfill_caused_by_heldout.py, and src/rebar/types.py was regenerated from the schemas (Dep gains NotRequired provenance). Review-bot advisory on the reopen-then-reclose-with-explicit-flag no-op keeping the original 'derived' marker: deliberate — bug 10d0 pins that confirming an already-linked target leaves the edge (and its link_uuid/timestamp) untouched; upgrading provenance would rewrite a proven-timestamp edge. Can be revisited as follow-up if escape-rate weighting needs it."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787452955651258001,"uuid":"a6df8510-c777-4731-a38e-f381aa88b25d"}